# Reviewed exceptions for `trivy config` (CI job iac-security). Each needs a reason.

# EKS public endpoint: enabled for GitHub-hosted runners, but restricted to
# var.api_allowed_cidrs (cluster_endpoint_public_access_cidrs). Trivy can't see
# through the terraform-aws-modules/eks input, so it reports it as unrestricted.
AVD-AWS-0040

# Worker node egress: nodes must reach ECR, STS and the EKS API; egress is
# open by design in terraform-aws-modules/eks. Ingress stays locked down.
AVD-AWS-0104

# Cloud SQL: ssl_mode = ENCRYPTED_ONLY already rejects non-TLS connections. The
# check wants client certificates too, which the app does not use (password over TLS).
AVD-GCP-0015
